#
# Settings for one Mac that serves oMLX behind Dynamo. setup.sh copies this file
# to ~/.config/dynamo-omlx/omlx-mac.env with a new API key; edit that copy.
# download_model.sh and service.sh source it with bash.
#
# Every Mac behind one Dynamo model needs the same model, OMLX_KV_BLOCK_SIZE and
# OMLX_API_KEY. oMLX itself also reads the variables named OMLX_* below.

# Hugging Face repo to download, and the oMLX model id served to Dynamo, which
# is the model's directory name under OMLX_MODEL_DIR.
OMLX_MODEL_REPO=Jundot/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-oQ4e-mtp
OMLX_BRIDGE_MODEL_ID=Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-oQ4e-mtp
OMLX_MODEL_DIR="$HOME/.omlx/models"

# Address the Linux proxies connect to. oMLX refuses a network address without
# an API key; the proxies send the same key (OMLX_API_KEY on Linux).
OMLX_HOST=0.0.0.0
OMLX_PORT=8000
OMLX_API_KEY=

# oMLX's SSD prefix cache, which the bridge mirrors into the Dynamo KV router.
OMLX_SSD_CACHE_DIR="$HOME/.omlx/cache"
# OMLX_SSD_CACHE_MAX_SIZE=200GB

# Tokens per cache block. For Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, oMLX picks 8192 on an M5 Mac
# with its native kernels and 2048 or 4096 elsewhere, and it only ever enlarges
# a preset, so presetting 8192 gives every Mac the same size. Prompt prefixes
# shorter than one block are not cached. Leave empty to let oMLX choose.
OMLX_KV_BLOCK_SIZE=8192

# Requests oMLX runs at once (oMLX's default is 8).
# OMLX_MAX_CONCURRENT_REQUESTS=16

# oMLX's multi-token prediction (MTP): speculative decoding in which the model's
# own MTP head drafts tokens that the model then verifies. on or off is written
# to oMLX's per-model settings before the model loads, and stays there; empty
# keeps what oMLX has, which is off unless its admin page turned it on. Macs
# behind one model may differ here.
# OMLX_MTP=on
# Most draft tokens per verify cycle, 1 to 8; an adaptive controller picks the
# depth up to this ceiling. Empty keeps oMLX's default, 3 for this model.
# Needs oMLX 0.7.0rc1 or later.
# OMLX_MTP_DEPTH=3

# Seconds `service.sh start` waits for the model to load, and seconds before
# service.sh restarts oMLX after it exits. The delay doubles, up to 300, while
# oMLX keeps exiting within a minute of starting.
# OMLX_START_TIMEOUT=1200
# OMLX_RESTART_DELAY=10

# Extra flags for the bridge and for `omlx serve`, separated by spaces.
# OMLX_BRIDGE_ARGS="--audit-interval 60"
# OMLX_SERVE_ARGS="--memory-guard safe"

# oMLX's Python, found automatically for Homebrew, the macOS app and pip installs.
# OMLX_PYTHON=/opt/homebrew/opt/omlx/libexec/bin/python

# Downloads. A Hugging Face token lifts the Hub's limits on anonymous downloads;
# `./download_model.sh --login` saves one without putting it in this file.
# HF_TOKEN=hf_...
# A mirror, plain HTTP when Hugging Face's Xet storage endpoints are unreachable
# from this network, and 0 to turn off the parallel Xet transfers that
# download_model.sh turns on.
# HF_ENDPOINT=https://hf-mirror.com
# HF_HUB_DISABLE_XET=1
# HF_XET_HIGH_PERFORMANCE=0
